Patch 6001: spu_lifter.py --data-range, lift_jobmods.py --table, SPU_ABI on the workload
registry's extern entry declarations.

spu_lifter.py --data-range START-END (repeatable) drops functions that start inside an embedded data range and caps a
function that runs into one at the range start (like --code-end, for islands). lift_jobmods.py --table TSV reads a
per-module lift table keyed on the module hash: mode=tail -> --code-end, head/island -> one --data-range per range,
drop_seed_base_plus_0x30=1 omits the base+0x30 seed. build_spu_workloads.py declares the lifted entries SPU_ABI so
the registry's calls match their definitions on Win64.
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: upstream split lift_jobmods.py main() into lift_module() and
module_seeds() (PR #444 verified regions, 7d8d507f link base from the header); the table lookup now lives in
lift_module() (TABLE is module-level, filled by main), the seed drop is a module_seeds() argument, and an explicit
code end (CODE_END or --engine-elf's reachability end) still wins over the table, as CODE_END did before.
spu_lifter.py and build_spu_workloads.py hunks unchanged (offsets only).

